				<string>The link adapter, and the only place the two-argument awkwardness lives. A shortcuts:// link carries ONE text string, so it can never hand over the two-item list Run-Pick wants. The payload is the argument that may contain anything, including newlines, so it cannot be a delimited field; the verb list is bounded, so it can. This takes the bounded one as input, reads the payload from the clipboard, pairs them, and calls Run-Pick. Run-Pick itself stays pipeable.</string>
